================================================================================
Third-party components
================================================================================

Telegrarr bundles/depends on the following open-source components. Each remains
under its own license; consult each project for authoritative terms.

Python dependencies
-------------------
  Telethon .............. MIT License        (MTProto client)
  cryptg ................ MIT License        (AES-NI crypto backend)
  FastAPI ............... MIT License        (web framework)
  Starlette ............. BSD-3-Clause       (ASGI toolkit, via FastAPI)
  Pydantic .............. MIT License        (validation, via FastAPI)
  Uvicorn ............... BSD-3-Clause       (ASGI server)
  Jinja2 ................ BSD-3-Clause       (templating)
  python-multipart ...... Apache-2.0         (form parsing)
  itsdangerous .......... BSD-3-Clause       (signed session cookies)
  bcrypt ................ Apache-2.0         (password hashing)
  httpx ................. BSD-3-Clause       (HTTP client)

All of the above are permissive licenses compatible with GPL-3.0.

Design & assets
---------------
  UI icons .............. Modeled on the Lucide (ISC) and Feather (MIT) open
                          icon sets; inlined as SVG (app/static/js/icons.js).
  Design tokens ......... Colour roles, radii, and type scale adapted from the
                          Open Design project's reference design systems
                          (github.com/nexu-io/open-design), Apache-2.0.
  Fonts ................. No proprietary fonts are redistributed. The CSS
                          references system fonts (e.g. "SF Pro" on Apple
                          platforms) with open fallbacks (Inter, Helvetica).

Third-party services (optional, used at runtime)
------------------------------------------------
  The Movie Database (TMDB) — poster/backdrop art via the TMDB API. Requires a
    user-supplied API key under TMDB's terms. "This product uses the TMDB API
    but is not endorsed or certified by TMDB."
  IMDb suggestion endpoint — keyless, unofficial/undocumented; best-effort.
  Plex — targeted library refresh via the Plex API on your own server.

